\title{The Master Theorem}
\date{2026-10-23T13:41:25Z}
\tag{algorithms}
\tag{draft}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{Adding up the total work in a recursion tree for divide-and-conquer algorithms can be generalized to a powerful theorem known as the \em{Master Theorem}.  (It is not named for someone; it is just a powerful theorem that "masters" a very wide range of divide-and-conquer algorithms. This is especially true when considering its generalizations such as the [Akra-Bazzi method](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akra-Bazzi_method).)}

